                "text": "Express both ground distances in terms of the height using tangent, then apply the cosine rule.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $O$ be the foot of the tower, with $OA=a$ and $OB=b$. From the two right-angled triangles:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan37^\\circ&=\\frac{h}{a}\\\\a&=\\frac{h}{\\tan37^\\circ}\\\\\\tan31^\\circ&=\\frac{h}{b}\\\\b&=\\frac{h}{\\tan31^\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nApply the cosine rule in $\\triangle AOB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}47^2&=\\left(\\frac{h}{\\tan37^\\circ}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{h}{\\tan31^\\circ}\\right)^2-\\frac{2h^2\\cos110^\\circ}{\\tan37^\\circ\\tan31^\\circ}\\\\h^2&=\\frac{47^2}{\\frac{1}{\\tan^237^\\circ}+\\frac{1}{\\tan^231^\\circ}-\\frac{2\\cos110^\\circ}{\\tan37^\\circ\\tan31^\\circ}}\\\\h&=\\frac{47}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{\\tan^237^\\circ}+\\frac{1}{\\tan^231^\\circ}-\\frac{2\\cos110^\\circ}{\\tan37^\\circ\\tan31^\\circ}}}\\\\h&\\approx19.12\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
